[SIZE=4][B]OpenRune migration and verification[/B][/SIZE]
OpenRune behavior is independently adapted to the existing Rust architecture and revision 239.1 target. It is not a drop-in plugin copy. Item definitions, interfaces and source/Wiki differences need explicit checks.

The migration ledger tracks implementation and registration. Independent verification checks exact builds and includes native actions, saved state and reference comparisons. Headless tests help, but do not replace playing through the native client. Prepared demonstrations use disposable accounts and seeded items; they do not prove those items can already be acquired normally.

The discovery inventory is a source-review list, not a gameplay completion percentage. Many obligations remain open, including native verification of newer content. The ordinary spade action is one recent implementation checkpoint; its quest and boss hooks are still unported.

